; The provider adapters: one module per adapter, the way
; [src/seekwright/providers/] is laid out, and every one of them satisfies
; [Seekwright.Provider.S].
;
; This is a separate library rather than a subdirectory of [seekwright] because
; [(include_subdirs qualified)] in the parent directory would not allow the
; [lib/caps/] stanza, and a library stanza here is the alternative that keeps the
; directory. The public name puts it inside the same artifact: findlib sees
; [seekwright.providers], the build sees [Seekwright_providers], and the opam
; package stays one.
;
; The dependency direction is the constraint worth remembering: these adapters
; depend on [seekwright] (the contract in [../provider.ml] and the wire models in
; [../model.ml]), never the reverse. Nothing in [lib/] may name an adapter, so
; the module that builds a name into a provider — Python's [factory._PROVIDERS] —
; needs its own stanza (P5) rather than a [lib/factory.ml] here, which would
; close a cycle.
(library
 (name seekwright_providers)
 (public_name seekwright.providers)
 (libraries seekwright mcp-caps uri yojson))
